# WP-CLI (Local)

For `http://selfieshowroom.local/`, do **not** call bare `wp` — Local MySQL needs the site socket.

## Use

```bash
cd wp-content/themes/sober-child
./bin/wp option get siteurl
./bin/wp theme list
./bin/wp plugin list
```

The wrapper selects Local’s PHP, MySQL unix socket, `--path` to `app/public`, and `--url=http://selfieshowroom.local/`.

## Requirements

- Local site **selfieshowroom** must be running
- System WP-CLI at `/usr/local/bin/wp` (falls back to Local’s `wp-cli.phar`)

## Do not

- Run plain `wp` from the theme or public dir (DB connection will fail)
- Edit `wp-config.php` only to make WP-CLI work
- Change parent theme / plugins via WP-CLI unless the user explicitly asks
